hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1393","Abu Musa Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna narrated to us, Mu’mal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ya’la bin Ata’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: “The sun eclipsed during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stood up and stood for a long time until it was said: He should not bow. Then he bowed and prolonged the bowing until it was said: He should not rise. Then he raised his head and stood for a long time until it was said: He should not prostrate. Then he prostrated and prolonged his prostration until it was said: He should not raise. Then he raised his head and sat until it was said: He should not prostrate. Then he prostrated, then he got up and did the same in the next time, then the sun set.”"
